    "turn_text": "there's two avenues that I think we should pursue. And the first is, conservatives need to stand up. You know, during the civil rights era, the civil rights leader is called on the people to boycott racist businesses. We have businesses that are suppressing conservative speech. We don't need to get next-day delivery from Amazon. We don't need to get our name out on Facebook. We don't need to use Amazon in Apple in the way that we are. And so I'll give you an example, turn off the tracking device on your phone. If you use Waze or Google Maps and you've got your location, turn it off so that they can't track you all over the place because they sell that information and they make a really good living off of where you are, what time, and what you've searched for. So that's one area is to make sure that as a consumer we're using our head. And then the other area are these antitrust bills which would create competition in the marketplace. So just like cable news, just like newspapers, we would have the ability to have choice for consumers.",
